# 29. BSOD TRIAGE
# ============================================================
#
# Kernel tasks MUST use BSOD_TRIAGE and DRIVER_REVIEWER.
#
# BSOD_TRIAGE should inspect:
#
#     BugCheck
#     bugcheck arguments
#     suspicious instructions
#     IRQL
#     memory lifetime
#     invalid pointers
#     use-after-free
#     double-free
#     race conditions
#     synchronization
#     pool usage
#     reference counting
#     IOCTL validation
#     user/kernel boundary
#     cleanup
#     device lifetime
#     interrupt handling
#     DMA assumptions
#     pageable/non-pageable correctness
#     exception paths
#
# Important:
#
# A crash location is NOT automatically the root cause.
#
# Correlate evidence.
#
# ============================================================
# 30. FIVE-PASS BSOD STATIC REVIEW LOOP
# ============================================================
#
# For kernel projects, execute FIVE independent static BSOD safety passes.
#
# The system must NOT simply ask one agent five times to say "looks good."
#
# Each pass must independently inspect the CURRENT source state.
#
# Pass:
#
#     1
#       ↓
#     identify issues
#       ↓
#     fix identified issues
#       ↓
#     2
#       ↓
#     identify issues
#       ↓
#     fix
#       ↓
#     3
#       ↓
#     identify issues
#       ↓
#     fix
#       ↓
#     4
#       ↓
#     identify issues
#       ↓
#     fix
#       ↓
#     5
#
# Each pass must record:
#
#     pass number
#     source revision
#     findings
#     evidence
#     fixes
#     remaining concerns
#     reviewer
#     result
#
# Continue until five consecutive completed passes report:
#
#     NO REMAINING IDENTIFIED BSOD-RELATED ISSUES
#
# Do NOT report:
#
#     "BSOD is impossible."
#
# Do NOT report:
#
#     "100% BSOD-proof."
#
# The correct claim is:
#
#     "Five independent static safety review passes completed with no
#      remaining identified BSOD-related issues."
#
# If a pass finds an issue:
#
#     fix it
#     invalidate the previous clean-pass streak
#     begin counting clean passes again.
#
# Example:
#
#     PASS 1 CLEAN
#     PASS 2 CLEAN
#     PASS 3 ISSUE FOUND
#     FIX
#     PASS 1 CLEAN
#     PASS 2 CLEAN
#     PASS 3 CLEAN
#     PASS 4 CLEAN
#     PASS 5 CLEAN
#
# Only then may the static BSOD review requirement be satisfied.
#
# ============================================================
